00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Obsession is a 1976 American neo-noir psychological thriller film directed by Brian De
Palma, starring Cliff Robertson, Geneviève Bujold, and John Lithgow.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
The screenplay was written by Paul Schrader, from
a story by De Palma and Schrader.

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Bernard Herrmann provided the film's soundtrack before his death in 1975.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
The story is about a prominent New Orleans businessman who is haunted by guilt following the
death of his wife and daughter during a kidnapping-rescue attempt gone wrong.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
Years later, he meets and falls in love with a young woman who
is the exact look-alike of his long dead wife.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
Both De Palma and Schrader have pointed to Alfred Hitchcock's Vertigo (1958) as the
major inspiration for Obsession's narrative and thematic concerns.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
Schrader's script  was extensively rewritten and pared down by De Palma before shooting, causing the
screenwriter to proclaim a complete lack of interest in the film's subsequent production and release.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
Completed in 1975, Columbia Pictures picked up the distribution rights but demanded that
minor changes be made to reduce potentially controversial aspects of the plot.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
When finally released in the late summer of 1976, it became De Palma's first
substantial box-office success and received mixed reviews from critics.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of sense of guilt, ransom, money
delivery, fake identity, florence, italy.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
